# VOCABULARY — the words that belong to the used-device-shop tenant and
# to no other tier (backlog be39298f).
#
# why: the same sensor that counts the brewery's words above the
# brewery (infra/lint/no-tenant-vocabulary-above-its-tier.sh) counts
# this tenant's, because on 2026-09-16 the measurement was not zero:
# `refurb` alone hit 193 times in core and modules — the refurb-used
# workflow's stage names in boss-jobs' registry, its policy defaults,
# and its step types seeded by core. A word here names nothing but this
# tenant, so a hit above the tenant tier is a leak by definition.
#
# Format: one term per line, matched case-insensitively. A trailing `*`
# matches any word beginning so; without it the term is a whole word.
# Terms are lowercase letters, digits, spaces and hyphens only.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: device (a webauthn or mobile device),
# diagnosis/diagnostic (CLAUDE.md §Diagnosis is about the pipeline),
# serial, service-account, repair — each names something outside this
# tenant.
refurb*
used-device*
used device*
